ts are added, and the incident report is complete and accurate.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787545458654},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating event validation**\n\nI’m working on creating a robust validation system and facing a malformed TypeError. There might be semantic sequence failures linked to that too. I need to ensure inputs are cloned before being queued so they don’t expose mutable internal states. It’s also crucial to determine the allowed payload keys, especially considering events like tradeId and version. Malformed inputs need to fit specific criteria, including non-emptiness and correct shapes, to avoid unsupported types which could also generate errors.**Streamlining callback handling**\n\nI need to improve how my project handles callback values since they're currently being ignored. I’m isolating callback arguments and working with snapshots for copies. Each trade gets its own queue to recover from rejections, making sure I avoid any poison in the queue. I can simplify the process by mapping tail promises for recovery, and cleaning up settled promises. Also, it's essential to validate that only the correct version of events is accepted while ensuring that duplicates or stale events don’t cause issues.**Handling version errors**\n\nI'm identifying a version gap error where versions greater than 1 are invalid if the first one isn't a CREATED event. When an event’s version is less than or equal to the current version, I should return a copy of the current without persistence, which might lead to unsupported events. Validation needs to happen upfront to catch unsupported or stale events, which would likely throw a TypeError. I also need to validate events structurally before dealing with the sequence, particularly for cancellations and new version rejections.**Implementing project adjustments**\n\nI’m working on refining another trade while staying focused on the committed aspects, like the student’s test state. There are five tests to consider. I realize that the async function clone is running synchronously, which affects how callbacks and mutations are handled. I’m thinking about returning the mutations and snapshots effectively. One thing to check is whether `structuredClone(event)` could be useful. Alright, I’ll go ahead and implement these changes!","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cyePEOE5NOE1oWBYAjeGFUXc","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs","content":"function copy(value) {\n  return value == null ? value : structuredClone(value);\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value) {\n  return value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction isValidNotional(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(value) && value > 0;\n}\n\nfunction isValidOwner(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim().length > 0;\n}\n\nfunction validateEvent(event) {\n  if (!isRecord(event)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event must be an object\");\n  }\n  if (typeof event.tradeId !== \"string\" || event.tradeId.trim().length === 0) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event.tradeId must be a non-empty string\");\n  }\n  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(event.version) || event.version < 1) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"event.version must be a positive safe integer\");\n  }\n  if (![\"CREATED\", \"AMENDED\", \"CANCELLED\"].includes(event.type)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`unsupported event type: ${String(event.type)}`);\n  }\n\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n    if (!isRecord(event.payload)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"CREATED requires a payload\");\n    }\n    if (!isValidNotional(event.payload.notional)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"CREATED requires a positive finite notional\");\n    }\n    if (!isValidOwner(event.payload.owner)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"CREATED requires a non-empty owner\");\n    }\n  } else if (event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    if (!isRecord(event.payload)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED requires a payload\");\n    }\n    const keys = Object.keys(event.payload);\n    if (\n      keys.length === 0 ||\n      keys.some((key) => key !== \"notional\" && key !== \"owner\")\n    ) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED may only replace notional or owner\");\n    }\n    if (\n      Object.hasOwn(event.payload, \"notional\") &&\n      !isValidNotional(event.payload.notional)\n    ) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED notional must be positive and finite\");\n    }\n    if (\n      Object.hasOwn(event.payload, \"owner\") &&\n      !isValidOwner(event.payload.owner)\n    ) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"AMENDED owner must be non-empty\");\n    }\n  } else if (\n    event.payload !== undefined &&\n    (!isRecord(event.payload) || Object.keys(event.payload).length !== 0)\n  ) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"CANCELLED payload must be empty when provided\");\n  }\n}\n\nfunction nextState(previous, event) {\n  if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n    return {\n      tradeId: event.tradeId,\n      version: event.version,\n      status: \"active\",\n      notional: event.payload.notional,\n      owner: event.payload.owner,\n    };\n  }\n  if (event.type === \"AMENDED\") {\n    return {\n      ...previous,\n      ...event.payload,\n      version: event.version,\n    };\n  }\n  return { ...previous, version: event.version, status: \"cancelled\" };\n}\n\nexport function createEventProjector(applyToStore) {\n  if (typeof applyToStore !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"applyToStore must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  const states = new Map();\n  const pendingByTrade = new Map();\n\n  async function project(input) {\n    let event;\n    try {\n      event = structuredClone(input);\n    } catch (cause) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"event must be cloneable\", { cause });\n    }\n    validateEvent(event);\n\n    const previousWork = pendingByTrade.get(event.tradeId) ?? Promise.resolve();\n    const operation = previousWork.then(async () => {\n      const previous = states.get(event.tradeId);\n\n      if (previous === undefined) {\n        if (event.version !== 1 || event.type !== \"CREATED\") {\n          throw new Error(\"the first event must be CREATED at version 1\");\n        }\n      } else {\n        if (event.version <= previous.version) {\n          return copy(previous);\n        }\n        if (event.version !== previous.version + 1) {\n          throw new Error(\"event version must be exactly the current version plus one\");\n        }\n        if (previous.status === \"cancelled\") {\n          throw new Error(\"a cancelled trade is terminal\");\n        }\n        if (event.type === \"CREATED\") {\n          throw new Error(\"CREATED is only valid as the first event\");\n        }\n      }\n\n      const candidate = nextState(previous, event);\n      await applyToStore(event.tradeId, copy(candidate), copy(event));\n      states.set(event.tradeId, candidate);\n      return copy(candidate);\n    });\n\n    // Keep the scheduling tail fulfilled so one failed operation cannot poison\n    // subsequent work for this trade. The caller still receives the rejection.\n    const tail = operation.then(\n      () => undefined,\n      () => undefined,\n    );\n    pendingByTrade.set(event.tradeId, tail);\n    void tail.then(() => {\n      if (pendingByTrade.get(event.tradeId) === tail) {\n        pendingByTrade.delete(event.tradeId);\n      }\n    });\n\n    return operation;\n  }\n\n  function getSnapshot(tradeId) {\n    return copy(states.get(tradeId) ?? null);\n  }\n\n  return { project, getSnapshot };\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":3,"output":2668,"cacheRead":4809,"cacheWrite":290,"reasoning":1278,"totalTokens":7770,"cost":{"input":0.000007500000000000001,"output":0.04002,"cacheRead":0.00120225,"cacheWrite":0.00090625,"total":0.042136}},"stopReason":"toolUse","